Changes and build scripts (in wasm/ of the package, and in the repository under core/utils-copyleft/wasm/)
  wasm/doom/build.sh
    the build: compiles the doomgeneric engine without its other platform layers and its SDL_mixer sound and music modules
  wasm/doom/doomecma.c
    new file, linked into the program: the platform layer, which draws the engine's frames into a window on SDL 3 and turns SDL key events into Doom keys
  wasm/doom/doomsound.c
    new file, linked into the program: the engine's sound module, a mixer that plays the sound effect lumps through an SDL 3 audio stream
  core/utils/wasm/lib/sdl.sh (in the repository; wasm/lib/sdl.sh and wasm/lib/sdl-gl/ in the npm package @ecmaos/coreutils)
    builds SDL as a static library for a Unix program on Wayland: a software window surface for its Wayland driver, audio and joystick drivers of its own, and the other changes its header lists
  core/utils/wasm/lib/wayland.sh (in the repository; wasm/lib/wayland.sh in the npm package @ecmaos/coreutils)
    builds libwayland-client, -cursor and -egl as static libraries, with listener calls made without libffi
  core/utils/wasm/lib/xkbcommon.sh (in the repository; wasm/lib/xkbcommon.sh in the npm package @ecmaos/coreutils)
    builds libxkbcommon as a static library without meson; a missing Compose table is logged at debug level

The changes were made in 2026; the repository history dates each one.

Toolchain: WALI's musl and the LLVM runtimes (musl 243ec00c3ffb910375db487d7eb24ea76d1e2c9f, LLVM 22.1.8), with the patches in utils/wali/patches;
utils/wali-version in the repository pins them, and utils/wali/build-sysroot.sh builds them. Its compiler then
puts a signal check in each loop of the linked program (utils/wali/signal-checks.mjs).

